  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 404 AM EDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nHot and humid. Highs will remain in the 90s through the long term. \nThe big concern with be the heat index values which will rise into \nthe triple digits through the work week. Expect apparent \ntemperatures between 100-105. Luckily, a front is set to take aim at \nthe area towards the end of the week. While temperatures will remain \nin the 90s, the front will help ease Heat Index values out of the \ntriple digits. \n\nScattered thunderstorms during the afternoon will continue through \nthe week, though it appears to be lowest on Wednesday and Thursday. \nBy the time the weekend rolls around, the front will dip far enough \nsouth to give us better chances for afternoon thunderstorms with a \nsource of lift present in the area. We'll need to keep an eye on the \ndeveloping dynamics through the week to keep an eye on the severe \nthreat, but as of right now there doesn't appear to be any sign of a \nsignificant outbreak.",
